{
  "name": "N42-N68-speech-session-scoped",
  "about": "ADR 0046 \u00a73b, N42/N37 on SpeechEvent (Rust only: Electron's helper recognises speech itself). A speech session that fails before the ack marks the part asr-unavailable; when the host respawns the part's session and it reaches ready, the flag clears and words land in the live transcript. Words held behind the ack are replayed in order (N37). Events naming another part's audio file are dropped; system-channel utterance ids stay apart from mic ids; speaker turns and loading status change nothing. N68: words on a channel the part's session was not started with are dropped (a channel is always given: it is typed).",
  "script": [
    {
      "op": "helper",
      "msg": {
        "type": "hello",
        "protocol": 1,
        "helperVersion": "test",
        "os": "macos",
        "features": []
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "helper",
      "msg": {
        "type": "permissions.status",
        "status": {
          "accessibility": "granted",
          "screen-recording": "granted",
          "microphone": "granted"
        }
      }
    },
    {
